Hi Jeff, Alexis

I know this is an old post but it's been useful for me in comparing density estimates from Distance. Unfortunately I don't have access to the Introduction to Distance Sampling book and I've been running t tests to compare density estimates between two sites using the code below:

n <- d1-d2
d <- sqrt(se1^2 + se2^2)
t <- n/d
df <- (se1^2*df1+se2^2*df2)/(se1^2+se2^2)
p <- pt(t,df)

d1/d2 =  density estimates from model output
se1/se2 = standard errors from model output
df1/df2 = degrees of freedom from model output

However my cv is very high in most cases and I'm struggling to understand how to incorporate this as you had mentioned below, is it a simple replacement of se for cv, and logging the densities?:

n <- log(d1) - log(d2)
d <- sqrt(cv1^2 + cv2^2)
t <- n/d
df <- (cv1^2*df1+cv2^2*df2)/(cv1^2+cv2^2)
p <- pt(t,df)

Thanks for your help
Kirstie

