Hi Carolin,

I created a custom version of plot.ds() from the code in mrds from a couple of years ago. The code is attached.

Please note that this is not code that you can just load and call from R. It is highly customized to my specific workflow, which does things like attach custom attributes to the object returned by ddf.ds() (although most of those are not relevant to the plotting you are interested in). If you try to simply copy and paste the function and just call it, it won’t work. Instead you should use it as an example and develop your own version of plot.ds. The code for plotting covariates in colors appear in lines 342-418.

It would be great if the distance developers had time to do something similar in the mrds package itself. Dave Miller has seen these plots before but I know his “to do list” is very long. I could eventually prepare a pull request of code that was properly generic if that was of interest to them. (This would be in September or later, as I am super busy until then.)

All the best,

Jason

